   "sentenceId": 12,
   "he": "וְלֹא הָיוּ לַבָּזִיכִין שׁוּלַיִים וְכוּ׳. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: כׇּל הַבָּזִיכִין שֶׁבַּמִּקְדָּשׁ לֹא הָיוּ לָהֶן שׁוּלַיִים, חוּץ מִבְּזִיכֵי לְבוֹנָה שֶׁל לֶחֶם הַפָּנִים — שֶׁמָּא יַנִּיחוּם וְיִפְרוֹס הַלֶּחֶם.",
   "en": "It was further stated in the mishna that «the bowls did not have» flat «bases.» The Gemara adds that «the Sages taught» a baraita that states: «None of the bowls in the Temple had» flat «bases» for the same reason, so that they should not be put down, which would allow the blood to congeal. This was «with the exception of the bowls of frankincense» that would be placed on «the showbread,» which did have flat bases. They could not have sharp bottoms out of concern that «perhaps» the priests «would rest them on the bread and the bread would break.» The showbread had an intricate and delicate shape, and a bowl with a sharp bottom could pierce or break the bread."
  }
 ],
